# The BigQuery plug's client side, for episode images built with
# `--warehouse-clients bigquery` (Dockerfile ALKERA_WAREHOUSE_CLIENTS): the
# Python client and the dbt adapter, both pointed at bigquery.internal:9050 (the
# audited proxy in front of the emulator) - the client with AnonymousCredentials
# and client_options api_endpoint, dbt-bigquery with method oauth-secrets, a
# static token and api_endpoint (warehouses.dbt_output; the proxy forwards no
# credential and the emulator checks none).
#
# dbt-bigquery requires google-cloud-bigquery[pandas] and nbformat, so pandas,
# pyarrow, nbformat and jupyter_core's `jupyter` dispatcher land in the image's
# system Python - on a de image too, where the notebook libraries are otherwise
# the da/ds roles' (toolbelt_check.py ROLE_IMPORTS / ROLE_BINARIES). Decision D2
# (2026-10-13): they ship as the client's hard dependencies, allowed by name in
# toolbelt_check.py CLIENT_IMPORTS / CLIENT_BINARIES the way Databricks' pandas
# and pyarrow are; the rest of the notebook stack (ipykernel, jupyter-server,
# nbclient, matplotlib) stays forbidden. `dbt seed` is a load job, which the
# proxy refuses by name.
#
# Held below 1.12, measured 2026-10-13: dbt-bigquery 1.12 lists every dataset's
# routines (routines.list) inside the same `try` that lists its tables, and
# catches NotFound there by returning no relations at all. The emulator does not
# serve routines.list ("unsupported bigquery.routines.list"), and the proxy
# answers it as an unknown route (404), so under 1.12 dbt's relation cache is
# empty for every dataset: an incremental model silently rebuilds as a table and
# a snapshot silently starts over. 1.11 lists tables only and needs the same
# dependencies. Lift the cap once the proxy answers routines.list truthfully (the
# emulator runs CREATE FUNCTION but cannot list or get the routine it made).
#
# Compiled here, NOT in pyproject/uv.lock, like every backend's clients
# (docker/lock_warehouse_clients.py): constrained to the base, native and ds
# locks, so every package it shares with them is the same version - pandas,
# pyarrow and nbformat are the da/ds images' own; certifi is the one deliberate
# exception (bigquery-clients.overrides). Regenerate with the command in
# requirements-bigquery.lock's header.
google-cloud-bigquery>=3.25,<4
dbt-bigquery>=1.9,<1.12
